[sub_resource type="RectangleShape2D" id="RectangleShape2D_kill"]
size = Vector2(8000, 40)

; Two gaps in the ground (players ring out through them) under a low
; ceiling that pins swing height well below open sky. Rewards a compact,
; controlled swing over the wide, open arcs a tall stage rewards.
;
; A hazard hangs from the centre of that ceiling (issue #18). The ceiling
; was already the thing that made this stage what it is -- it is what stops
; you swinging over the gaps in a single wide arc -- but it was only a
; limit, something you bumped into. The hazard makes the middle of it
; hostile, so the highest, fastest line across the stage is now the one
; that kills you, and a crossing has to be either low and slow over a gap
; or wide around the centre.
;
; Hung from the ceiling rather than laid on GroundMid, which was the other
; obvious placement. GroundMid is only 200 px wide and the hazard is 160,
; so laying it there would leave two 20 px slivers of safe ledge -- the
; one place in the stage you land after a committed swing would become a
; coin flip. A hazard belongs in the space you cross, not the space you
; land on.

